SELECT BookID, Title
FROM BOOKS
WHERE Author = 'A. Haider';

SELECT SUM(Copies)
FROM BOOKS
WHERE Genre = 'History';

SELECT PatientID, Name
FROM PATIENTS
WHERE Insured = FALSE;

SELECT COUNT(*)
FROM PATIENTS
WHERE BloodGroup = 'O+';

SELECT Item, Price
FROM PRODUCTS
WHERE Category = 'Drinks';

SELECT COUNT(*)
FROM PRODUCTS
WHERE Category = 'Grocery' AND Stock > 0;

SELECT SUM(Rainfall)
FROM WEATHER
WHERE Country = 'Pakistan';

SELECT Title, Minutes
FROM MOVIES
WHERE Genre = 'Comedy';

SELECT FilmTitle, StartTime
FROM SCREENINGS
WHERE Is3D = TRUE AND ScreenNo = 2;

Any three explained, e.g.
- auto-documenter: produces documentation/explanations of the code automatically, so other team members can understand and maintain it;
- prettyprint: consistent colour coding and indentation, so code written by different people is easy to read;
- error diagnostics: identify and highlight errors and their position, so bugs are found quickly;
- run-time environment / breakpoints / stepping: run and pause the code to watch variable values, so logic errors can be traced;
- auto-correction: fixes common typing errors automatically, reducing syntax errors;
- auto-completion: suggests identifiers, so names are used consistently.

Any three explained in context, e.g.
- managing system security / user accounts: each member of staff logs in with their own account and password, so only authorised staff can see patient records;
- file management: the OS organises records into folders, controls opening, saving, copying and deleting, and sets access rights so records are not changed by the wrong people;
- handling interrupts: urgent signals (e.g. a device error) are dealt with immediately so systems keep working;
- memory management: each application has its own memory so one program cannot corrupt another;
- managing peripherals: drivers let the computers use printers/scanners for records.

Any three, e.g.
- SSL/HTTPS: encrypts data sent between browser and server, so intercepted account details cannot be read;
- two-step verification: a code is sent to the customer's phone, so a stolen password alone does not give access;
- firewall: filters traffic to the bank's servers, blocking unauthorised access/hacking attempts;
- anti-malware on servers: detects and removes malware that could steal data;
- access levels: staff only see the customer data needed for their job;
- automatic logout/session timeouts: an unattended session is closed;
- proxy server: hides internal server addresses and filters requests.
